# ---------------------- 9. Notes for downstream analysis ---------------------
# tracer_positions.dump holds per-step positions/velocities of the 2*Ntrace
# "particles of interest" only. In Python:
#   1. project onto an arbitrary detection direction q to mimic the DHM
#      scattering vector:      phase_j(t) = q . r_j(t)
#   2. sum partial waves        E(t) = sum_j exp(i*phase_j(t))   (homodyne)
#      or add a fixed reference term for a heterodyne analogue
#   3. Fourier-transform the field/intensity autocorrelation (Wiener-
#      Khinchine) to obtain a DPD-generated S(omega), for comparison
#      against the CTRW/Levy Monte Carlo spectra and DHM bench data.
#
# Unit mapping back to physical units follows Basan et al. 2011, Table 2:
#   t_ref = 1 day, l_ref = 10 um, p_ref = 1000 Pa (rescale as needed for
#   your organelle speed/persistence-time targets from Nolte 2024, Table 2).
